<title>UK: Scottish &amp; Newcastle shares up on profit.</title>
<headline>Scottish &amp; Newcastle shares up on profit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scottish &amp; Newcastle Plc, the UK's biggest brewer, saw its shares rise 7-1/2 pence to 657 1/2 on Monday after reporting a 21 percent rise in year pretax profits.</p>
<p>Pretax and pre-exceptional profits were 374 million stg, within the range of 361 million to 380 million forecast by analysts.</p>
<p>&quot;It's pretty much in line with what we predicted,&quot; said one analyst. S&amp;N said the results reflected strong sales in food and key beer brands in the second half of the year.</p>
</text>
